course: dictionary
lesson: 12790
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is right. «Eject» is one of these words. «Press eject before you pull out the USB stick.» Here eject means to take something out of a machine safely.
explain: «The volcano ejected ash and hot rock into the sky.» Ejected means pushed out with force. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try push out in place of ejected, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The referee ejected the player for a rough tackle.» Ejected means made to leave a place, often by force. The clues are referee and rough tackle, which are about rules and trouble in a game, not about machines.
explain: Pilots also eject from a plane in an emergency. They are shot out of the plane in a special seat. The meaning is still about being pushed out with force, but the place and the reason change it.
fact: Eject is a verb: eject, ejects, ejected, ejecting.
fact: «Eject» can mean to push or throw something out with force.
fact: «Eject» can mean to make someone leave a place, often by force.
fact: «Eject» can mean to take a disc, cartridge or memory stick out of a machine, or to tell a computer you are removing it.
fact: A pilot can eject from a plane in an emergency, using a special seat that shoots them out.
exercise: «Press eject before you pull out the USB stick.» What does eject mean here? | Wash it in water | Lose it under the desk | Push it in harder | *Take it out of the computer safely
exercise: «The volcano ejected ash and hot rock into the sky.» What does ejected mean? | Melted quietly | Cooled down slowly | Hid under the ground | *Pushed out with force
exercise: Which word in «The referee ejected the player for a rough tackle.» tells you the player had to leave the game? | tackle | referee | *ejected | player
test: «The pilot ejected safely from the damaged plane.» What does ejected mean here? | Flew the plane faster | Painted the plane a new colour | *Escaped by being shot out of the plane | Landed the plane gently
test: Mia says eject only means taking out a disc. Why is she wrong? | Eject means to be quiet and still | Eject means to put something inside a machine | *Eject can also mean to push something out with force, or to make someone leave
exam: «The angry fan was ejected from the stadium.» What does this mean? | *Made to leave by force | Given a free ticket for the next match | Invited to sit in the best seats | Asked to buy a drink
